From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: keep DRIVER_GEM_GPUVA -- 6.18.36 still gates on it

The mainline driver imported by `drm-imagination-carry-the-mainline-driver` does not set DRIVER_GEM_GPUVA. That is
correct upstream and wrong here, and the difference is one line of drm core:

  mainline  drm_gem.c:235   drm_gem_gpuva_init(obj);
  6.18.36   drm_gem.c:195   if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_GEM_GPUVA))
                                    drm_gem_gpuva_init(obj);

Upstream made the init unconditional and then dropped the now-pointless flag
from pvr_drv.c. Importing that file into 6.18.36 therefore leaves
obj->gpuva.list with .next == NULL for every PowerVR GEM object.

MEASURED, not reasoned backwards from: a run on the 8 GiB board, first ioctl that
walks the list:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffffffffffffffd8
  pc : drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked+0x4c/0x16c [drm_gpuvm]
  lr : pvr_vm_map+0xf8/0x2bc [powervr]
  x19: ffffffffffffffd8

0xffffffffffffffd8 is NULL - 0x28, and 0x28 is offsetof(struct drm_gpuvm_bo,
list.entry.gem) -- i.e. list_for_each_entry() in drm_gpuvm_bo_find() doing
container_of() on a NULL list head. Not a corrupted pointer: an uninitialised
one.

Blast radius of the flag in this tree is exactly two call sites,
drm_gem.c:195 and the "gpuvas" debugfs node (drm_debugfs.h:51). No other
driver's behaviour changes.

The alternative -- backporting the drm core change that makes the init
unconditional -- would touch every DRM driver in the tree to fix one. This
does not.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
@@ -1379,7 +1379,7 @@
 DEFINE_DRM_GEM_FOPS(pvr_drm_driver_fops);
 
 static struct drm_driver pvr_drm_driver = {
-	.driver_features = DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_RENDER |
+	.driver_features = DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_GEM_GPUVA | DRIVER_RENDER |
 			   DRIVER_SYNCOBJ | DRIVER_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE,
 	.open = pvr_drm_driver_open,
 	.postclose = pvr_drm_driver_postclose,
